hi i'm eric voss and the mandalorian on  disney plus is an  excellent star wars series with a  misleading title the series was first  pitched as the story of a solo  gunslinger but when the first episode  premiered  we all learned very quickly that it was  so so much more  thanks to little green baby jesus now i  get why the creative team wanted to  hide this reveal it was pretty amazing  but really this series deserves to be  titled something like  baby yoda and the mandalorian because  it's not about the mandalorian by  himself it's about his  relationship with this little nugget  without the child i don't think we'd be  that interested in the show  but why is the connection between these  two characters so endearing to us  despite one being a puppet and the other  being a faceless best scar helmet  i'm gonna break down the unique nature  of the relationship between mando and  baby yoda  with some interesting visuals and  choices that the people who made these  episodes  snuck in there to make us root for these  two so hard  and freak out anytime they're separated  okay so when mando and baby yoda first  meet  their relationship seems to take  inspiration from the manga and film  series  lone wolf and cub a weary traveling  warrior forced to escort an adorable  moppet  who ends up teaching him a thing or two  we've seen versions of this duo and  other media  and yeah we've seen it a bit in star  wars stories but what makes mando and  baby yoda different is the kind of  accidental way they come together like  there's no assignment from higher  authorities or destiny  mando is a violent killer who took on a  gig to find a bounty and was totally  prepared to kill it but at the last  second he  softens and the whole mystery of the  series from then on is why  why does mando love this kid and why  again and again does he sacrifice  the little he has why does he throw  himself in harm's way  ought to protect this stranger a  stranger whom he has no idea the  significance of since he doesn't know  anything about yoda or the jedi order  now we should say this doesn't seem like  too huge a mystery to us as we're  watching it  like as viewers if we found an adorable  kid we would  probably feel some sense of paternal and  tribalistic duty to keep it safe but in  the context of the show it's worth  remembering that the universe of star  wars is  horribly cruel to children nearly every  kid we meet in this universe has a real  shitty life  young anakin skywalker and those kids on  canto bight in the last jedi are  slaves young jen erso young rey young  mando they're  refugees from war the young lanes of the  jedi temple i guess had it okay for a  bit but really only because the jedi  sought out force sensitive kids across  the galaxy and highly  pressured their parents to give away  these kids to their cult  so they would never see their parents  again and then at the end of it all the  kids got  wrecked during order 66 so how good was  the jedi order for them  so really mando has no practical reason  to care for baby yoda  the kid brings nothing but trouble into  his life and indeed mando very nearly  gives baby yoda away to a client who  intends to kill it but then halfway  through episode 3  mando makes a big choice he goes back  into burner her socks compound  on navarro and john wicks his way  through stormtroopers to bust this kid  free and escape with him  it is a fully impractical insane  decision one that violates  everything about his bounty hunter code  and it only makes sense  as the decision made for love so again  why does mando love baby yoda why do any  of us love anything  what is love baby odor don't have meat  on him well for my  limited experience i feel confident in  telling you that  love is best described as the feeling of  home see human beings evolved as tribal  creatures we cling closely to warm  campfires and familiar kin  and then as we wander away into our  lives away from the campfire we are  always in search of a new campfire  a new tribe and we only feel love when  we feel at home  again and don't get too impressed or  sentimental i'm just romanticizing  rick's depressing tape listen morty i  hate to break it to you but what people  call love  is just a chemical reaction that compels  animals to breed it hits hard morty then  it slowly fades  leaving you stranded in a failing  marriage i did it your parents are gonna  do it  break the cycle morty rise above focus  on science happy valentines  but both rick sanchez and mando are lone  wolves who  out of love cling to their tribes and  this  need for tribe is at the core of the  mandalorian  mando lost his family as a young boy but  he was saved by a group of mandalorians  and they  in a sense became his adopted tribe he  offers whatever earnings he makes back  to his tribe as a kind of tribute but he  still doesn't quite fit in  he comes into conflicts with other  members of the tribe and his armorer  reminds him that he has not yet selected  a signet  a signet representing the inner clans of  the mandalorian people  well that all changes when he meets baby  yoda baby yoda reminds mando of his  own beginnings the visuals reinforce the  parallel nature of their origins  remember mando began as a kid hiding  behind shutter doors  from a killer droid before getting saved  by a stranger in a mandalorian helmet  baby yoda  also hides behind shutter doors and is  saved at the last minute  when mando shoots ig-11 mando as a boy  got flown away from conflict  peering over the shoulder of his  mandalorian savior baby yoda is depicted  in the same angle in the final episode  and the way baby yoda's face reflects  from mando's chrome helmet  mando sees his reflection in the child  they are both orphans from war  both survivors thanks to the mercy of a  warrior so mando realizes that baby oda  might be the only person who could ever  truly understand him  season one shows us mando's transition  from the tribe he was adopted into  to the tribe he chooses for himself  early episodes established him as an  outer tier general member of the  mandalorian tribe but by the end of the  season he has transitioned  into his new tribe which the armorer  calls the clan  of two and the final minutes make this  new tribe official  with the item that mando gives baby yoda  the mythosar skull  the ancient crest of the mandalorian  people it once hung kind of like a  banner in  mando's former home the tunnels of  navarro now it's with his new home  the family that he loves so whenever we  hold our breath in terror when baby oda  gets put in danger and then  exhale a sigh of relief when he's back  in amanda's arms it's not just because  the kid is an adorable huge  precious pee it's because we know how  much mando needs him  and i don't care how intense the  affection is between joker and harley  quinn or falcon winter soldier rick and  morty scarlet witch and vision  no one needs each other as much as those  two do  [Music]  you
 

